From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS branding: product name, device name, installer

- The OS is NickelOS (IDS_PRODUCT_OS_NAME, IDS_SHORT_PRODUCT_OS_NAME,
  IDS_INSTALLED_PRODUCT_OS_NAME), so setup, the installer and Settings say
  NickelOS instead of ChromiumOS.
- A generic device is a "NickelOS device" ("Welcome to your NickelOS
  device") instead of a "Chrome device", Google's product name.
- The installer's introduction drops the g.co/flex links and Google's
  disclaimer for a free-software one, and the installer and "Install or
  try" screens show a computer instead of Google's logo.

Only the English strings change; other locales keep their translations
of the old text until NickelOS has its own.

diff --git a/ash/login/resources/ash_login_strings.grd b/ash/login/resources/ash_login_strings.grd
index e98bc3690bbf4..a19d87a2fe8a8 100644
--- a/ash/login/resources/ash_login_strings.grd
+++ b/ash/login/resources/ash_login_strings.grd
@@ -2637,13 +2637,13 @@
         Installing <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph> will overwrite all data on your device.
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_OS_INSTALL_SCREEN_INTRO_CONTENT_0" desc="First part of body text of the OS install screen's introduction step.">
-        Before starting, make sure you have a backup of your data. Installing <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph> will overwrite your hard drive. Learn more at g.co/flex/InstallGuide.
+        Before starting, make sure you have a backup of your data. Installing <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph> will overwrite the disk you choose.
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_OS_INSTALL_SCREEN_INTRO_CONTENT_1" desc="Second part of body text of the OS install screen's introduction step.">
         Installation takes a few easy steps. You’ll have another chance to confirm before changes are made to your computer.
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_OS_INSTALL_SCREEN_INTRO_FOOTER" desc="Footer text of the OS install screen's introduction step.">
-        Google isn’t responsible for any data loss, and <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph> may not work on uncertified models. Learn more at g.co/flex/InstallGuide.
+        <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph> is free software provided as is: it may not work on every computer, and its authors are not responsible for any data loss.
       </message>
       <message name="IDS_OS_INSTALL_SCREEN_INTRO_NEXT_BUTTON" desc="Text of the next button on the introduction page of the OS install screen">
         Install <ph name="DEVICE_OS">$1<ex>ChromeOS Flex</ex></ph>
diff --git a/chrome/app/chromium_strings.grd b/chrome/app/chromium_strings.grd
